  "_bit_split_comment": "Multi-bit R/W registers split into per-bit entities (read-modify-write). kind: button = momentary set-only trigger, switch = persistent on/off bit, status = read-only binary. mask = max writable word (validates writes). slug/key -> uid <prefix>_<slug>, translation key foxair_<key> in strings.json + en/de/ru + icons.json. select.py skips these addrs; switch.py/button.py/binary_sensor.py build entities generically from metadata (format=bit_split).",
  "bit_split": {
    "1016": {
      "mask": 5,
      "bits": {
        "0": {"kind": "button", "slug": "manual_defrost", "key": "manual_defrost", "icon": "mdi:snowflake-alert"},
        "2": {"kind": "button", "slug": "manual_heating_boost", "key": "manual_heating_boost", "icon": "mdi:fire"}
      }
    }
  },
  "_alias_switch_comment": "Normal-mode switches backed by a plain register (not a bit word): key -> entity foxair_<key>, uid <prefix>_<key>. Purpose-built to expose an expert-block control (e.g. H22 silent enable) without ungating the whole block. Switch reads addr (on = raw == on_value) and writes on/off values.",
  "alias_switch": {
    "8801": {"key": "pv_surplus", "on": 4, "off": 2, "icon": "mdi:solar-power-variant", "category": "primary"}
  },
  "_pv_surplus_comment": "pv_surplus: HEMS-facing switch (EVCC Home Assistant switch, HA automations) on the virtual SG input 8801. on = SG mode 4 High PV, off = SG mode 2 normal. Only acts while SG01 (1334) = 3 Modbus. The unit applies a new SG mode at most every 10 min (FoxAir_Control docs/sg_ready.md), 8801 reads back at once, SG status 2133 shows the accepted mode.",
  "_non_expert_comment": "Expert-block addrs exposed in normal mode (merged into CORE_NON_EXPERT_ADDRS at build). H user settings; H30 excluded (installer-only, expert).",
